---
import type {RevisedCapability} from '../data/capabilityRedesign';
import {inquiryInputs} from '../data/capabilityRebuild';
import {orderConditions} from '../data/capabilityRedesign';
import {libraryGuide} from '../data/resourceLibrary';
import CapabilityIntro from './CapabilityIntro.astro';
import CapabilityEvidence from './CapabilityEvidence.astro';
import CapabilityPartFigure from './CapabilityPartFigure.astro';
import CapabilityMaterialTable from './CapabilityMaterialTable.astro';
import CapabilityApplications from './CapabilityApplications.astro';
import CapabilityDecisionGuide from './CapabilityDecisionGuide.astro';
import {capabilityDecisions} from '../data/capabilityDecisions';
import '../styles/multi-axis.css';
interface Props {page:RevisedCapability;quoteHref:string}
const {page,quoteHref}=Astro.props;
const guide=capabilityDecisions[page.slug];
// The other process routes use their own narratives; this route explains
// indexed access versus continuous contour motion.
const parts=page.parts.filter(part=>part.product.slug!=='global-manufacturer-of-multi-sided-precision-machined-components');
const checks=page.acceptanceChecks.map(row=>row.feature==='Features across faces'?{...row,drawing:'Hole and bore axes, mounting interfaces and relative positions.'}:row);
---
<div class="axis-page pn-capability-rollout" data-penta-capability={page.slug}>
 <div data-core-section="service"><CapabilityIntro page={page} quoteHref={quoteHref}/></div>
 <section class="axis-section axis-routing" id="geometry-review" data-core-section="route-and-setup">
  <header><h2>{page.plan.geometry.title}</h2><p>{guide.featureIntro}</p></header>
  <div class="axis-routing-grid"><div><dl class="axis-route-list"><div><dt>Indexed positioning</dt><dd>Hold the rotary axes at a selected orientation to reach an angled face. Relate features across faces to the same datum scheme.</dd></div><div><dt>Simultaneous motion</dt><dd>Change orientation along a continuous contour. The model, tool reach and fixture clearance determine whether this route is needed.</dd></div></dl><div class="axis-envelope"><h3 id="size-and-setup-review">Size and workholding</h3><p>{page.overview.workholding}</p><p>Send finished and blank dimensions, known weight and protected clamping areas. Machine travel, load, orientation and fixture limits are assessed per drawing.</p></div></div><CapabilityEvidence id="five-axis-machine-wide" caption="The spindle, workpiece and rotary setup show the space needed for tool access. Original LZZ photograph; it does not establish simultaneous motion, travel, load or finished acceptance." sizes="(max-width:767px) 300px, 340px"/></div>
  <CapabilityDecisionGuide slug={page.slug}/>
  {page.study&&<a class="rd-link" href={page.study.href}>{page.study.title}</a>}
 </section>
 <section class="axis-section axis-forms" id="part-examples" data-core-section="forms-and-features">
  <header class="axis-heading"><h2>{page.plan.exampleHeading}</h2><p>{page.plan.exampleIntro}</p></header>
  <div class="axis-form-layout" id="machining-studies"><div class="axis-source-group"><CapabilityEvidence id="five-axis-parts" caption="Original component forms from the multi-axis source group." sizes="(max-width:767px) 220px, 260px"/><p>Bores, holes and working faces reached from different directions need a common datum scheme. The drawing sets their positional and profile requirements.</p></div><div class="axis-example-list">{parts.map(part=><article><CapabilityPartFigure part={part} linked={false} showCaption={false}/><div><h3><a href={part.href}>{part.title}</a></h3><p>{part.text}</p></div></article>)}</div></div>
  <div class="axis-related"><p class="rd-note">Specify surface roughness, permitted tool marks and the required inspection records.</p><p>Also review <a href="/machined-parts/gallery/custom-billet-aluminum-engine-cover-manufacturer-and-automotive-prototype-supplier/">contoured billet covers for assembly checks</a> and <a href="/machined-parts/gallery/global-manufacturer-of-multi-sided-precision-machined-components/">multi-face components</a>.</p></div>
 </section>
 <div class="axis-section axis-materials" data-core-section="materials"><CapabilityMaterialTable page={page} intro={guide.materialsIntro}/></div>
 <section class="axis-section axis-quality" id="engineering-fit" data-core-section="inspection">
  <header class="axis-heading"><h2>Measure against the model and datums</h2><p>{page.overview.inspection}</p></header>
  <table class="rd-table rd-stacked axis-checks" id="capability-scope"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Feature</th><th scope="col">Specify on the drawing</th><th scope="col">Agree before production</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(row=><tr><th scope="row">{row.feature}</th><td data-label="Drawing">{row.drawing}</td><td data-label="Before production">{row.inspection}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
  <aside class="axis-tests"><h3>{page.scopeQuestions[0].question}</h3><p>Balance, leak, rotor validation and other functional tests need separate procedures and acceptance limits. Include final end use and applicable export requirements with the request.</p></aside>
  <div class="axis-quality-context"><CapabilityApplications slug={page.slug} textOverrides={{'Industrial fans & impellers':'Review blade hubs and rotating forms for tool access, material and inspection requirements.'}}/><CapabilityEvidence id="cmm-room" caption="Original LZZ CMM photograph. Confirm current range, calibration and measurement capability from equipment records." sizes="220px"/></div><a class="rd-link" href="/factory/#quality">Inspection methods, stages and records</a>
 </section>
 <section class="axis-section axis-rfq" id="enquiry" data-core-section="quotation"><header><h2>{page.plan.rfqTitle}</h2></header><div class="axis-rfq-grid"><ul>{inquiryInputs[page.slug].map(input=><li>{input}</li>)}</ul><aside><p id="order-conditions">{orderConditions}</p><a class="rd-button" href={quoteHref}>Request a quote</a><p class="rd-note">Review the draft, then add your drawings and send it from your email app.</p><a class="rd-link" href={libraryGuide('rfq-checklist').href}>RFQ preparation checklist</a></aside></div></section>
</div>
